{
  "version": "0.1-draft",
  "date": "2026-11-03",
  "notes": [
    "US personal-mail taxonomy derived from research/mail.md (Azure Document Intelligence and Google Document AI prebuilt models as evidence that fields are stable; IRS i1099gi for recipient deadlines; IRS record-keeping rules for retention).",
    "Edits versus the raw report: every secret identifier is a last-4 placeholder (Class A secrets never leave the archival PDF); micr_routing removed; marketing mail is archived forever and hidden by default instead of purged (the founder's requirement is that every captured paper stays digitally available).",
    "retention_basis 'convention' means practitioner convention rather than law; the app shows retention as guidance, never as legal advice.",
    "keep_original true means the app announces 'keep this paper' at capture."
  ],
  "cross_cutting_fields": ["envelope_required", "keep_original", "sensitive", "junk"],
  "classes": [
    {"class": "tax.w2", "doc_type": "tax_form", "examples": ["W-2", "W-2c"], "key_fields": ["employer", "employer_ein", "employee_tax_id_last4", "tax_year", "box1_wages", "box2_fed_withheld", "state_wages"], "action": "keep_for_tax_year", "due": "recipient copy by Jan 31", "retention": "tax_year+7y", "retention_basis": "IRS 3/6/7-year rules, use max", "sensitive": true, "junk": false},
    {"class": "tax.1099", "doc_type": "tax_form", "examples": ["1099-NEC", "1099-MISC", "1099-INT", "1099-DIV", "1099-B", "1099-R", "1099-G", "1099-K", "1099-S", "1099-SA", "1099-Q", "1099-C", "1099-OID", "1099-DA", "SSA-1099"], "key_fields": ["payer", "payer_tin", "tax_year", "variant", "box_amounts", "recipient_name"], "action": "keep_for_tax_year", "due": "Jan 31; B/DA/S/LS/SB by Feb 15", "retention": "tax_year+7y", "retention_basis": "IRS", "sensitive": true, "junk": false},
